UPDATE companies SET description='Pristine Surgical, based in Manchester, New Hampshire, is a medical device company focused on simplifying endoscopy through single-use visualization systems. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year or original founders; its board includes representatives from Piney Lake Capital Management, a private equity firm.

The company’s flagship product is the Summit™ 4K single-use surgical arthroscope, a sterile, ready-to-use rigid endoscope that eliminates reprocessing, maintenance contracts, and sterilization delays. Pristine pairs the hardware with Pristine Connect®, a cloud-based platform that automates inventory management, stores images and video, and provides digital training checklists. A subscription model, branded Scopes as a Subscription™, replaces capital equipment purchases with predictable per-procedure pricing. The product pipeline extends to laparoscopy and flexible endoscopy, targeting a global addressable market of 125 million procedures annually.

Pristine serves hospital operating rooms, ambulatory surgery centers, and orthopedic practices. Early adopters include Southern California Orthopedic Institute, UCLA, Hospital for Special Surgery, Virtua Health in New Jersey, Doral Surgery Center in Florida, and Stetson Lee Orthopaedics in California. The company’s advisory board comprises surgeons specializing in shoulder, knee, elbow, and sports medicine.

Pristine was started to remove inefficiency, variability, and safety risks from the endoscopy suite. By delivering a new high-definition scope for every case, the company aims to reduce staff exposure to contaminated instruments, accelerate room turnover, and provide transparent, automated economics for surgical visualization.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design and manufacture of single-use rigid endoscopes (arthroscopes)", "Development of flexible endoscopes", "Cloud-based surgical visualization software (Pristine Connect)", "Subscription-based equipment and supply management", "Automated inventory management", "Digital training and checklists"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Surgical visualization", "Orthopedics", "Arthroscopy", "Laparoscopy", "Flexible endoscopy", "Sports medicine"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-use 4K endoscopes eliminate reprocessing and maintenance", "Subscription pricing with automated inventory management", "Cloud-based Pristine Connect software for image/video sharing and training", "New sterile scope for every procedure", "Predictable transparent per-procedure pricing"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Manchester, New Hampshire -> db", "Flagship product: Summit\u2122 4K single-use surgical arthroscope -> /", "Cloud platform: Pristine Connect\u00ae -> /", "Subscription model: Scopes as a Subscription\u2122 -> /", "Product pipeline: arthroscopy, laparoscopy, flexible endoscopy -> /", "Advisory board surgeons: Getelman, McAllister, Snyder, Williams -> /", "Customer examples: SCOI, UCLA, HSS, Virtua, Doral, Stetson Lee -> /", "Executive team: McKillop, Goodchild, Abrams, Seger, Snyder -> /about", "Board members: Booth, Cleary, Matlin, Lazar (Piney Lake) -> /about", "Mission: simplify endoscopy, remove inefficiency/variability/safety risks -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Pristine Surgical is a medical device company with a mission to simplify endoscopy.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pristine-surgical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pro Form Metals operates a family-owned fabrication shop on Dickerson Road in Reno, Nevada.

The shop produces custom chimney caps, fireplace surrounds, seamless gutters, kitchen range hoods, interior accents, railings, gates, and general brackets, guards, and caps. Work includes welding, forming, and cutting to spec for both one-off pieces and production runs. The company also supplies cut-to-length metal roofing panels and locally fabricated trim and flashings, though it does not perform roof installation.

Customers include builders, contractors, and homeowners in Reno, Sparks, Truckee, Carson City, Dayton, Fernley, Incline Village, Minden-Gardnerville, and the broader Lake Tahoe area. Projects range from residential kitchen hoods and chimney caps to commercial railings and architectural accents.

