UPDATE companies SET description='Prysmian Group USA is headquartered in Houston, Texas. The U.S. operating unit of the global Prysmian Group was established in 2005, though the parent company traces its roots back 150 years in cable manufacturing. The group operates in over 50 countries and employs approximately 34,000 people worldwide, with more than 15,000 in the United States.

The company manufactures power, data, and telecommunication cables for electrical utilities, telecommunications providers, and industrial customers. Its product portfolio includes high-voltage transmission cables, submarine cable systems, low-carbon aluminum cables, and hollow-core fiber for AI-ready data centers. Manufacturing facilities are located in Texas and other states, supporting a diversified production footprint across the group''s global network.

Prysmian serves the utilities, oil and gas, telecommunications, and data center sectors. Its cables are used in power grid transmission, digital infrastructure, electrification projects, and renewable energy installations such as wind farm interconnections.

The company emphasizes a diversified business model across geographies and product lines, coupled with a focus on low-carbon cable technologies to reduce the environmental footprint of digital and energy infrastructure.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Power cable manufacturing", "Data cable manufacturing", "Telecommunication cable manufacturing", "Submarine cable system production", "Hollow-core fiber manufacturing", "Low-carbon aluminum cable production", "High-voltage transmission cable production", "Renewable energy cable solutions"], "industries": ["Utilities", "Oil & Gas", "Telecom", "Data Centers", "Power Transmission", "Digital Infrastructure", "Electrification", "Renewable Energy"], "materials": ["Aluminum (low-carbon)", "Copper", "Optical fiber"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Houston, Texas -> db", "Founded in 2005 -> db", "Employee count 15000+ in US -> db", "Global employee count 34,000 -> page /", "Operates in 50+ countries -> page /", "150 years of experience -> page /", "Produces power, data, and telecommunication cables -> db", "Manufacturing facilities in Texas -> db", "Serves utilities, oil & gas, telecom, data centers -> db", "Markets: Transmission, Digital Solutions, Electrification, Power Grid -> page /", "Low-carbon aluminum cables for AI infrastructure -> page /", "Hollow-core fiber for AI-ready data centers -> page /", "Xtera acquisition for submarine telecom -> page /", "Aurubis strategic partnership -> page /", "Atkore acquisition approved -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Prysmian Group is a global cable manufacturer. In the U.S., produces power and specialty cables for electrical utilities, telecom and industrial applications.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "15000+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='prysmian-group-usa' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Cheyenne, Wyoming, Puma Steel has operated for decades across the Western United States as a structural steel fabricator and supplier. The company serves Colorado, Wyoming, and surrounding states from its Cheyenne yards, where it maintains thousands of tons of steel inventory.

Puma Steel provides a full range of steel services including structural and miscellaneous steel fabrication, design-build, design-assist, steel supply, pre-processing, project management, in-house BIM modeling, engineering, detailing, value engineering, erection, and LEED documentation. The firm dedicates in-house engineers, project managers, and quality specialists to each project, and its fabrication capacity is supported by large yard stock.

The company works primarily with general contractors on commercial, healthcare, education, and government projects. Notable examples include the 1144 Fifteenth office tower in Denver (GC Hensel Phelps), the Utah Data Center at Camp Williams, the Marian H. Rochelle Gateway Center at the University of Wyoming (GC Haselden Construction), and medical centers such as Platte Valley Medical Center and Lutheran Medical Center.

Puma Steel emphasizes communication, professionalism, and safety as differentiators. It holds AISC certification as a fabricator since 1997, maintains AWS-certified welding inspectors, and operates an award-winning safety program. The firm also offers non-destructive testing (NDT Level I and II) including liquid penetrant, magnetic particle, and ultrasonic inspection, along with sophisticated paint coating endorsements (P1, P2, P3).', certifications=ARRAY['AISC Certified Fabricator (Since 1997)','AWS Certified Welding Inspectors','American Society of Non-destructive Testing – NDT Level I and II','Liquid Penetrant Testing','Magnetic Particle Testing','Ultrasonic Testing','Standard for Steel Building Structures','Sophisticated Paint Coating Endorsement P1, P2, & P3']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Miscellaneous steel fabrication", "Design-build", "Design-assist", "Steel supply", "Steel pre-processing", "Project management", "In-house BIM modeling", "In-house engineering", "In-house detailing", "Value engineering", "Erection", "LEED documentation", "Non-destructive testing (NDT Level I/II)", "Liquid penetrant testing", "Magnetic particle testing", "Ultrasonic testing", "AWS certified welding inspection", "Sophisticated paint coating (P1, P2, P3)"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Education", "Government", "Commercial construction", "Data centers"], "materials": ["Structural steel", "Miscellaneous steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AISC Certified Fabricator since 1997", "In-house BIM modeling, engineering, and detailing", "Thousands of tons of steel inventory in Cheyenne yards", "Award-winning safety program", "LEED documentation support"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Cheyenne, Wyoming -> db", "Decades of experience in Western U.S. -> db", "Services: fabrication, project management, BIM modeling, engineering, in-house detailing, design build, design assist -> /", "Thousands of 