UPDATE companies SET description='PwrQ is based in Hanover, Maryland, and traces its roots to 1926. The company is now part of Forgent, a platform that brings together over a century of experience in power infrastructure.

PwrQ designs and manufactures low-voltage power distribution equipment, including its S1 switchboard line, remote power panels (RPP), panelboards (120/208 V to 600 V), and power distribution units (PDU) with integrated monitoring. The company operates vertically integrated facilities that handle raw copper busbar fabrication, CNC turret punching, laser cutting, robotic welding, and final assembly and test. Dedicated production lanes for each product family enable high-volume, high-precision output. A planned 220,000-square-foot expansion near the current headquarters will add capacity.

The company serves hyperscale data centers, manufacturing plants, utility and grid operators, hospitals, and other mission-critical facilities. Its engineering teams support projects from utility service entrance to rack-level load, while field service crews provide preventive maintenance, commissioning, retrofits, and generator solutions (3 kW to 10 MW) across the U.S.

PwrQ emphasizes that vertical integration gives it control over quality, lead times, and capacity. Dedicated lanes and AI-driven machinery aim to reduce variability and accelerate throughput. The firm also highlights its end-to-end engineering capability—spanning single-line design, selective coordination, arc-flash studies, and SCADA/BMS integration—as a differentiator for complex, fast-paced projects.', certifications=ARRAY['UL Listed']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Power systems engineering", "Reliability studies", "Short circuit coordination", "Arc flash studies", "Switchgear controls and automation", "SCADA/BMS implementation and integration", "Generator paralleling", "Hybrid microgrid controls", "Preventive maintenance of MV/LV switchgear, breakers, relays, transformers", "Generator maintenance", "Start-up and commissioning", "Systems integration", "Training programs", "Retrofits and upgrades of legacy electrical equipment", "Copper busbar fabrication", "CNC turret punching", "Laser cutting", "Robotic welding", "Automated copper processing", "Final assembly and test", "Low voltage switchboard (S1) manufacturing", "Remote Power Panel (RPP) manufacturing", "Panelboard manufacturing (120/208V to 600V)", "Power Distribution Unit (PDU) manufacturing", "ATS unit manufacturing"], "industries": ["Hyperscale data centers", "Manufacturing facilities", "Power grid / utilities", "Hospitals / healthcare", "Industrial facilities", "Mission-critical environments"], "materials": ["Copper busbar"], "equipment": ["CNC turret punches", "Laser cutters", "Robotic welders", "Automated copper processing systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated manufacturing from raw copper busbar to final tested assembly", "Dedicated production lanes for each product family (switchboards, RPPs, PDUs, panelboards)", "Advanced machinery fleet including CNC turret punches, laser cutters, robotic welders, automated copper processing", "AI-ena