UPDATE companies SET description='Quantum Imaging operates as SCD USA Infrared LLC, a U.S. subsidiary of Israel-based Semiconductor Devices (SCD), from its headquarters in Colorado Springs, Colorado. The company leverages more than four decades of infrared detector development and manufacturing experience accumulated by its parent organization.

The company designs and manufactures infrared detectors and camera cores across the short-wave (SWIR), mid-wave (MWIR), and long-wave (LWIR) spectral bands. Its product lines include the Blackbird, Cardinal, Bird, and Pelican families, offered as integrated detector dewar cooler assemblies (IDDCAs) and complete camera engines. Manufacturing encompasses III-V semiconductor material growth, VLSI read-out integrated circuit design, and environmental qualification testing for harsh defense environments. Tens of thousands of detectors have been produced for deployment.

Primary customers operate in defense, aerospace, security and surveillance, and commercial sectors. Defense programs include airborne, land, naval, and missile applications such as intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance (ISR), missile warning, and situational awareness. A noted example is a 2020 agreement to supply Raytheon with SWIR cameras and optical sensor packages. Commercial applications span aviation safety, gas sensing, non-destructive testing, semiconductor inspection, and process monitoring. Space imaging is also served.

The company states its mission is to deliver innovative, field-ready, intelligent imaging and detection systems that enable real-time visualization of mission-critical intelligence in all theaters and environments. It differentiates itself through a broad product portfolio, scalable engine and camera architectures, and the integration of artificial intelligence and machine learning with infrared sensor technology.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 14001:2004','OHSAS 18001','ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Infrared detector manufacturing", "SWIR camera core manufacturing", "MWIR camera core manufacturing", "LWIR camera core manufacturing", "Integrated Detector Dewar Cooler Assembly (IDDCA) manufacturing", "VLSI design", "Infrared semiconductor material development", "Environmental qualification testing", "AI/ML integration for infrared imaging", "Cooling capability"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Security & Surveillance", "Commercial", "Space", "Homeland Security", "Industrial"], "materials": ["InSb", "XBn", "InGaAs", "Type II SuperLattice (T2SL)", "Vanadium Oxide (VOx)"], "equipment": ["BLACKBIRD 640", "SPARROW", "MINI BLACKBIRD 1280", "BLACKBIRD 1280", "CARDINAL 640", "CARDINAL 640 Low Noise (LOON)", "CARDINAL 1280", "BIRD 640", "BIRD XGA", "PELICAN D LW ENGINE", "QI-SWIR-HD10"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Broadest product offering in the infrared detector industry", "Scalable engine and camera architecture for diverse mission requirements", "World-class III-V semiconductor material and VLSI design expertise", "Environmental qualification for demanding defense and space applications", "Integration of AI and machine learning with infrared sensing"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Colorado Springs, CO -> /about-us", "US subsidiary of Israel-based SCD (Semiconductor Devices) -> /", "Manufactures tens of thousands of infrared detectors and imaging solutions -> /", "Product lines: Blackbird, Cardinal, Bird, Pelic