UPDATE companies SET description='REM Electronics Supply Company, Inc. operates from Warren, Ohio, where it was founded in 1955 by Robert E. Miller. The business began as a sales and service operation focused on consumer-market TV antennas and hi-fi equipment before evolving into a broader electronics supplier.

Today the company provides full contract manufacturing, assembly, testing, and distribution from a combined office and warehouse footprint of 30,000 to 75,000 square feet. Its manufacturing services cover surface-mount and through-hole PCB assembly, cable and wire-harness assembly, 3D printing and prototyping, design assistance, component preparation and modification, X-ray inspection, and RFID integration.

REM serves U.S. government agencies involved in defense and national security, as well as manufacturers, assemblers, and repair teams across the electronics sector. The company emphasizes its ability to source or recreate obsolete and hard-to-find components to prevent production downtime.

The firm highlights its domestic production as a differentiator, stating that U.S.-based manufacturing ensures higher quality control, faster turnaround, and stronger supply-chain security for the defense customers it supports. Leadership frames the mission as honoring the founder’s legacy through competitive pricing and a commitment to customer service.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract manufacturing", "SMT assembly", "Through-hole assembly", "Cable and wire harness assembly", "Testing", "Distribution", "3D printing and prototyping", "R&D and design assistance", "Component preparation and modification", "X-ray inspection", "RFID integration", "Obsolete and hard-to-find parts sourcing"], "industries": ["Defense", "Government"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 70 years of continuous operation since 1955", "30,000\u201375,000 sq ft of office and warehouse space in Warren, Ohio", "Specializes in sourcing and replacing obsolete or hard-to-find electronic components", "U.S.-based manufacturing supporting defense and national security agencies"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1955 by Robert E. Miller -> /about", "Headquarters Warren, Ohio -> db", "Facility size 30,000+ sq ft -> /", "Facility size 75,000 sq ft -> /about", "Capabilities include contract manufacturing, assembly, testing, distribution -> /", "Specializes in obsolete and hard-to-find parts -> /", "Supports U.S. government defense agencies -> /", "Offers SMT and through-hole assembly -> /services", "Offers cable and wire harness assembly -> /services", "Offers 3D printing and prototyping -> /services", "Offers R&D and design assistance -> /services", "Offers component preparation and modification -> /services", "Offers X-ray inspection -> /services", "Offers RFID -> /services", "70 years in business as of 2025 -> /", "Builds in the USA -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products":