UPDATE companies SET description='RMC Plastics is headquartered in Houston, Texas. The company traces its roots to 1966 when three friends — B.L. Jacquet, L.L. ''Mack'' McKay Jr., and J.F. Cox — founded JMC Plastics and Manufacturing in the garage of McKay’s home. The operation later moved to its current north Houston site. Mack McKay bought out his partners and expanded the facility. After his death in 2003, his nephew Randy Hammond ran the company until 2012. In 2013 the McKay family sold the business to the Robertson family, also of Houston, and the firm was renamed RMC Plastics, Inc. The company remains family-owned and emphasizes direct owner involvement.

RMC Plastics specializes in precision plastic and rubber injection molding, offering end-to-end services from product and mold design through material consulting, production, assembly, and warehousing. The shop runs 12 injection molding machines of varying sizes, enabling large production runs and quick changeovers. The company also maintains a deep stock of customers’ proprietary parts in its Houston warehouse for rapid fulfillment. All production is domestic, with a focus on made-in-the-USA components.

The company serves a diverse industrial base across Texas and nationwide, including consumer products, oil and gas, electric, gas, and water utilities, construction, plumbing, and medical sectors.

The current ownership highlights its family-owned structure as a differentiator, stating that customers work directly with owners who can make fast, flexible decisions. The firm also emphasizes its domestic manufacturing footprint and its ability to guide material selection and tooling strategy to meet budget and deadline requirements.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Rubber molding", "Mold design", "Product design", "Material consulting", "Production", "Assembly", "Warehousing"], "industries": ["Consumer Products", "Oil & Gas", "Electric Utility", "Gas Utility", "Water Utility", "Construction", "Plumbing", "Medical"], "materials": ["Thermoplastics", "Rubber"], "equipment": ["Haitian International injection molding machines", "Nissei Plastic injection molding machines", "Borche injection molding machines", "ENGEL injection molding machines", "Moretto automation equipment", "Van Dorn Demag injection molding machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned with direct owner involvement", "12 injection molding machines with quick changeover capability", "Warehousing of customer proprietary parts for rapid fulfillment", "Made in the USA production", "Material consulting and mold design services"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1966 by B.L. Jacquet, L.L. ''Mack'' McKay Jr., and J.F. Cox -> /about-us", "Originally operated out of garage, relocated to north Houston -> /about-us", "Sold to Robertson family in 2013, renamed RMC Plastics -> /about-us", "Operates 12 injection molding machines -> /about-us", "Industries served: Consumer Products, Oil & Gas, Electric Utility, Gas Utility, Water Utility, Construction, Plumbing, Medical -> /about-us, /", "Warehousing of customer proprietary parts for quick turn-around -> /", "Family-owned with direct owner involvement -> /about-us", "Made in the USA production -> /", "Material consulting and mold design services -> /", "Brands of machiner