UPDATE companies SET description='Randy''s Booth Co. Inc. operates from Crystal, Minnesota, a northwest suburb of Minneapolis. The business traces its roots to the 1970s when Randy Kissoondath, an immigrant from Trinidad and Tobago, began building restaurant booths and established a national reputation through word of mouth. The firm has remained family-owned through two generations.

The company manufactures custom hospitality furnishings — booths, chairs, stools, tables, banquettes, and headboards — from Northern Hardwoods including cherry, ash, oak, and maple. A team of 20 craftspeople works in a renovated facility on two acres that the company moved into in September 2017. The building provides 20-foot ceiling clearance, a loading dock, a showroom, and combined office and production space that Bert credits for improved throughput and profitability.

Designers, architects, and builders across the United States specify Randy''s Booth for restaurant, lounge, healthcare, corporate office, and residential projects. Long-standing accounts include hotel chains such as Hyatt and Perkins, and local landmarks like Mancini''s Char House, Nye''s, and O''Gara''s. Recent work includes custom booths and furnishings for the Nova Restaurant Group''s Hazelwood Food & Drink and multiple concepts for restaurateurs Kam Talebi and Luke Derheim.

Bert Kissoondath says the company was built on his father''s insistence that everything be handmade and that pride in workmanship shows in the finished product. That philosophy earned the firm the 2024 Minnesota Manufacturer of the Year award and the SBA''s Minnesota Family Owned Business of the Year honor. Clients cite the team''s integrity, on-time delivery, budget adherence, and willingness to value-engineer as reasons they return.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom booth manufacturing", "Chair manufacturing", "Stool manufacturing", "Table and base manufacturing", "Banquette fabrication", "Headboard fabrication", "Woodworking with Northern Hardwoods", "Custom furniture design", "Installation services", "Value engineering", "Project management"], "industries": ["Restaurants", "Lounges", "Healthcare", "Corporate Offices", "Residential"], "materials": ["Cherry", "Ash", "Oak", "Maple", "Northern Hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Second-generation family ownership with hands-on leadership", "Full design-through-installation capability for custom hospitality furnishings", "National client base built on word-of-mouth reputation since the 1970s", "2024 Minnesota Manufacturer of the Year and SBA Family Owned Business of the Year"], "facts_used": ["Location: Crystal, Minnesota -> /about-us", "Founder: Randy Kissoondath, immigrant from Trinidad and Tobago, started in 1970s -> /about-us", "CEO: Bert Kissoondath (son), took over after father''s death in 2009 -> /about-us", "Family-owned business -> /about-us", "Products: custom booths, chairs, stools, tables, banquettes, headboards -> /", "Materials: Northern Hardwoods (Cherry, Ash, Oak, Maple) -> /", "Employee count: 20 -> /about-us", "Facility: 2 acres, 20-foot ceilings, loading dock, showroom, moved September 2017 -> /about-us", "Industries served: restaurants, lounges, healthcare, corporate offices, residential -> /", "Clients: Hyatt, Perkins, Mancini''s Char House, Nye''s, O''Gara''s, Nova Restaurant Group (Hazelwood), Kam Talebi, Luke Derheim -> /, /about-us", "Awards: 2024 Minnesota Manufacturer of the Year, SBA Minnesota Family Owned Business of the Year -> /, /about-us", "Philosophy: handmade quality, pride in workmanship -> /about-us", "Client testimonials on integrity, on-time delivery, budget adherence, value engineering -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our work includes high quality, expertly designed commercial booths, chairs, and tables made from Northern Hardwoods such as Cherry, Ash, Oak and Maple.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "20", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='randy-s-booth-co-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ray Brothers Inc., doing business as Ray Bros., Inc., operates from New Orleans, Louisiana. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed in the available sources.

The firm specializes in architectural sheet metal fabrication, producing structural panels (including the MT240 profile), architectural panels, and framing products. Its shop offers custom fabrication, waterjet cutting, and press forming, and it also provides commercial general contracting, material sales, and project planning, estimating, and design services. No facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures are published.

Ray Bros. serves commercial, institutional, and public-sector clients across the Gulf Coast. Completed projects include re-roofing the Nashville Avenue Terminal at the Port of New Orleans, retro-framing the Plaquemines Parish Council Building, copper roofing for the Old Algiers Court House and Holy Name of Mary Catholic Church, and roof retrofits for Fifth Ward Elementary, Slidell Government Tower, and the Louisiana Avenue Wharf.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Fabrication", "Waterjet Custom Cutting", "Press Forming", "Commercial General Contracting", "Material Sales", "Project Planning, Estimating and Design", "Structural Panels (MT240)", "Architectural Panels", "Framing Products"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Government/Municipal", "Education", "Religious institutions", "Port/Marine facilities"], "materials": ["Copper", "Prefinished painted metal"], "equipment": ["Waterjet cutting system", "Press"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Multiple metal roof profiles", "Custom fabrication capabilities", "Industry-leading prefinished paint systems", "Waterjet custom cutting", "In-house press forming"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in New Orleans, Louisiana -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label) and homepage", "Architectural sheet metal fabrication -> homepage", "Structural panels MT240, architectural panels, framing products -> homepage", "Custom fabrication, waterjet cutting, press forming -> homepage", "Commercial general contracting, material sales, project planning/estimating/design -> homepage", "Project examples: Port of New Orleans, Plaquemines Parish Council Building, Old Algiers Court House, Holy Name of Mary Catholic Church, Fifth Ward Elementary, Slidell Government Tower, Louisiana Avenue Wharf -> homepage", "Multiple metal roof profiles, custom fabrication capabilities, prefinished paint systems -> description"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": 