UPDATE companies SET description='Red Cloud Renewable Energy Center operates from Pine Ridge, South Dakota, as a 501(c)(3) nonprofit dedicated to energy sovereignty for Native American communities. The organization’s founding year and individual founders are not publicly disclosed, but its structure is rooted in community-led empowerment rather than private ownership.

The center delivers free, hands-on training in solar photovoltaic installation, weatherization, and sustainable building practices. Each training cohort completes live installations on homes of families in need, turning education into immediate community benefit. The organization does not publish facility size, headcount, or annual installation volume.

Programs serve Native American students seeking careers in renewable energy and households on tribal lands facing high energy costs and harsh weather. The work spans workforce development, residential solar deployment, and home resilience — all framed under the banner of energy sovereignty.

Leadership frames the mission as a “new way to honor the old ways,” linking cultural values to modern clean-energy skills. The model aims to foster self-sufficiency, lower utility bills, and cut emissions — roughly 1.5 tons of CO₂ per kilowatt installed — while building a Native-led solar workforce.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic installation training", "Weatherization training", "Sustainable building practices training", "Residential solar panel installation", "Workforce development for renewable energy"], "industries": ["Energy Sovereignty"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Free solar installation training for Native American students", "Every training class installs panels on homes of families in need", "Triple impact: workforce development, household energy relief, emissions reduction", "Curriculum covers solar PV, weatherization, and sustainable building practices"], "facts_used": ["Location: Pine Ridge, South Dakota -> db", "Legal status: 501(c)(3) nonprofit -> /", "Mission: empower Native American communities through solar installation, weatherization, sustainable building education -> /about", "Free training for Native students in solar installation and weatherization -> /", "Each class installs panels for families in need -> /", "Each kW installed prevents ~1.5 tons CO2/year -> /", "Focus on energy sovereignty -> db", "No founding year, founders, headcount, facility size, volume, equipment, certifications, materials, lead times, tolerances, CAGE code, min order, export compliance, languages, or social links stated -> /, /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Red Cloud Renewable is a 501(c)(3) organization that empowers Native American communities by offering vital education in solar installation and weatherization techniques.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "",