UPDATE companies SET description='Reed Manufacturing Co. Inc. was founded in 1919 by three brothers—Rex, Bob, and A.K. Reed—in a Tupelo, Mississippi warehouse as a dry-goods business. The company was rebranded Reed Manufacturing Co. in 1959 and transitioned to employee ownership in 2014 after a buyout of the Reed family.

The company designs and manufactures workwear including flame-resistant shirts, poly-cotton crew shirts, food-service coats, and enhanced-visibility garments. Production moved offshore in 2007, with facilities in the Dominican Republic (Ginatex and Overseas Jeans Co.), while customization, embroidery, RFID tagging, and reflective-tape application are performed at its Tupelo distribution center. Reed also operates a proprietary inventory-management system that supports consignment programs and forecasting for distributors.

Reed serves industrial, utility, food-processing, and safety-focused markets through a wholesale distributor network. Long-standing customers have included Mission Linen (consignment partner since 1986) and formerly major retailers such as JCPenney, Sears, and Mervyn’s. The product line spans FR-rated GlenGuard shirts, ANSI-compliant reflective apparel, and private-label uniform programs.

The founders’ original vision—high-quality garments, fair pricing, timely delivery, and unshakable integrity—remains the stated differentiator. Reed emphasizes its dual heritage in fashion and uniform apparel, low-minimum custom garment design, and a 50-year-old inventory system that reduces freight costs and stock obsolescence.', certifications=ARRAY['ANSI']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Flame-resistant garment manufacturing", "Poly-cotton blend garment manufacturing", "Food service coat manufacturing", "Enhanced visibility garment manufacturing", "Garment customization (reflective tape application)", "Hemming", "Pocket addition", "Embroidery and emblem sewing", "RFID chip integration", "Custom garment design and sourcing", "Private label manufacturing", "Inventory management and forecasting", "Consignment program management", "Distribution and warehousing"], "industries": ["Industrial workwear", "Flame-resistant clothing (oil & gas, electrical, utilities)", "Food processing and service", "Enhanced visibility safety apparel (construction, roadwork)", "Uniform rental and laundry", "Wholesale distribution"], "materials": ["Polyester", "Cotton", "Poly-cotton blend (65/35)", "Spun polyester (7.2 oz)", "Flame-resistant fabrics (GlenGuard)", "100% Cotton"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary inventory management system with forecasting and consignment capabilities", "Local customization at Tupelo distribution center (130+ retrofit codes)", "Custom garment design with extremely low minimums", "ANSI-rated FR and non-FR reflective tape application", "Employee-owned since 2014"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1919 by Rex, Bob, and A.K. Reed in Tupelo, Mississippi -> /about", "Employee-owned since 2014 -> /about", "Manufactures FR shirts, poly-cotton crew shirts, food service coats, enhanced visibility shirts -> /", "Customization services: reflective tape, hemming, pockets, embroidery, RFID -> /services", "Inventory management system with forecasting and consignment -> /services", "Facilities in Dominican Republic (Ginatex, Overseas Jeans Co.) -> /about", "ANSI-rated reflective tape -> /services", "Low minimums for custom garments -> /services", "Materials: 65/35 poly-cotton, 7.2 oz spun poly, GlenGuard FR fabrics -> /", "Headquarters Tupelo, Mississippi -> db", "Certification: ANSI -> db", "Former retail customers JCPenney, Sears, Mervyn''s -> /about", "Consignment partner Mission Linen since 1986 -> /about", "Transition offshore completed 2007 -> /about", "Company renamed Reed Mfg Co. 1959 -> /about", "Ed Nelson became CEO 1994 -> /about", "Zeb Atkinson became President & CEO 2020 -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "REED has designed and manufactured high quality, comfortable, protective workwear since 1919.", "founded_year": "1919", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "Extremely low minimums", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='reed-manufacturing-co-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Reeves Custom Metals Inc operates from Wichita, Kansas, where it was founded in 1897 as Reeves Brothers Blacksmith Shop in the city’s Delano district. The business remains family-owned, now in its fifth generation, and is located at 116 North Osage, one block north of the original site.

The shop provides full-service welding and custom metal fabrication, including high-definition plasma cutting, laser cutting, waterjet cutting, tube laser cutting, shearing, sawing, press brake forming, sheet and plate rolling, flame cutting, and CNC plasma shape cutting. It also offers AutoCAD design, general and machine repair, and weld processes such as arc, gas, MIG, and TIG. The company stocks a wide range of metals—steel, stainless steel, aluminum, copper, brass, and specialty alloys—and sells remnants with no minimum order quantity; out-of-stock items are typically replenished in one to two days.

Reeves Custom Metals serves customers across various industries in Kansas and beyond, though specific sectors are not detailed in its public materials. Its capabilities support fabrication, cutting, forming, and welding needs for both small and large orders.

