UPDATE companies SET description='Reworx operates from Morris, Connecticut, with a shop in nearby Watertown. The company was founded by a family team, though the exact year is not publicly stated. The founders, referred to as family founders, built the business around giving new life to reclaimed materials, starting with barn wood mantels and expanding into custom furniture and accents.

The company designs and builds custom furniture pieces using reclaimed wood, primarily sourced from old barns. Its services include a design studio where clients collaborate with reclamation experts, a salvage and wood sales operation for DIY projects, and a mobile onsite design-install consultation service for both residential and commercial spaces. The workshop and studio handle projects of varying scale, though specific production volumes and headcount are not disclosed.

Reworx serves homeowners, interior designers, and commercial clients seeking sustainable, story-rich furnishings. Examples include residential mantle installations and commercial space consultations. The company also caters to DIY enthusiasts through its reclaimed material sales.

Reworx distinguishes itself by merging sustainability with craftsmanship, transforming discarded materials into pieces that carry narrative weight. The founders emphasize innovation, quality, and environmental responsibility, aiming to combine timeless style with modern function.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Reclaimed material sourcing", "Onsite design installation", "Salvage wood sales", "Design consultation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "DIY"], "materials": ["Reclaimed wood", "Barn wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom furniture crafted from reclaimed barn wood", "Design studio collaboration with reclamation experts", "Mobile onsite design-install service for homes and businesses", "Salvage wood sales for DIY projects", "Commitment to sustainability and environmental responsibility"], "facts_used": ["Company name Reworx -> db", "Headquarters in Morris, Connecticut -> db", "Creates custom furniture and accents from reclaimed materials -> /", "Offers design studio collaboration, salvage wood sales, mobile onsite design install -> /", "Family founders -> /", "Shop location in Watertown, CT -> /", "Studio location in Morris, CT -> /", "Serves residential and commercial clients -> /", "Emphasizes sustainability and craftsmanship -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "At Reworx, we create custom furniture and accents that merge sustainability with exceptional craftsmanship.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='reworx' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rhino Wire Works operates from Delavan, Wisconsin, where it was established in January 1994 by John Burgstede as JB Wire Service, Inc. Burgstede brought over 40 years of experience from his uncle''s wire forming and stamping business, joined by George Jeninga for a combined 70-plus years in the trade. The company was acquired in 2024 by Jonathan Zepeda, who adds two decades in steel and metals, while Burgstede remains involved in operations.

The shop specializes in custom wire forms, handling projects from prototype through production runs for OEM and service parts. Its core capability is wire bending, quoting from prints, sketches, or samples, and it also designs and builds custom paint-line fixtures and hooks—sold under the Rhino Hooks brand—to increase line density and solve hanging issues. For secondary operations such as machining or finishing, the firm coordinates with local machine shops.

