UPDATE companies SET description='Rockford Molded Products traces its roots to 1943, when Henry "Hank" Gustafson and Norman Johnson opened a tool-and-die shop in a garage on 18th Avenue in Rockford, Illinois. The pair produced components for the U.S. Army during World War II, and by the 1950s they had built their first injection molding machine from scratch, laying the groundwork for a plastics-focused operation. Today the company is headquartered in Loves Park, Illinois.

The shop provides injection molding, product assembly, Bridgeport milling, custom fabrication, quality control, and 3D printing services. Its quality management system is certified to ISO 9001:2015 and is UL-approved, with calibration and documentation traceable to NIST standards.

The company serves a range of industrial customers, though specific sectors are not listed on its public pages. Its early work for the military suggests defense-related experience, and its current capabilities target manufacturers needing molded parts, machined components, and assembly.

